# You almost certainly do not need this file.
#
#     pip install 'bismuth-kb[parsers,server]'
#     bismuth
#
# That opens a browser and asks you four questions. It is the supported path, and
# it is better than this file: you pick a provider, paste a key, and Bismuth asks
# that provider which models your key can actually reach — so there is no model
# name to look up and no prefix to get wrong. Answers are saved to
# ~/.bismuth/config.json.
#
# This file is for Docker, CI, and anyone who would rather not use a browser.
# Everything below is optional and overrides the wizard's answers.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One rule worth knowing
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bismuth reads BISMUTH_* and nothing else. Putting OPENAI_API_KEY here does
# nothing at all — use BISMUTH_API_KEY.
#
# That looks unhelpful and is deliberate. Provider variables get set once, years
# ago, and forgotten; a tool that quietly prefers whatever it finds in your
# environment over what you just typed cannot tell you why it is failing. (Ask us
# how we know.) The BISMUTH_ prefix cannot collide with anyone else's leftovers,
# so what you set is what runs.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Models
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# provider: anthropic | openai | ollama | custom
# Model names are bare — the provider prefix is added for you.

# BISMUTH_PROVIDER_ID=anthropic
# BISMUTH_API_KEY=
# BISMUTH_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# Fully local: no key, nothing leaves the machine.
# BISMUTH_PROVIDER_ID=ollama
# BISMUTH_API_BASE=http://localhost:11434
# BISMUTH_MODEL=qwen3:14b

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vault -- the directory Bismuth organises. This is the source of truth.
# Delete .bismuth/ inside it and nothing of value is lost; it is a cache.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BISMUTH_VAULT_PATH=./vault

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BISMUTH_HOST=127.0.0.1
# BISMUTH_PORT=8765

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tuning. Every one of these has a working default; reach for them only when you
# have a reason. They are listed so you know they exist, not so you set them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A local single-GPU box wants 1; hosted APIs tolerate more.
# BISMUTH_LLM_MAX_CONCURRENCY=12

# How many documents may be read and summarised ahead of the one being filed.
# Reading is parallel; filing stays strictly ordered, because where a document
# goes depends on the folders the ones before it created.
# BISMUTH_INGEST_READ_AHEAD=8

# Silence after the last stream chunk, and a separate wall-clock ceiling that
# continuous output cannot reset. Per-task output caps normally stop first.
# BISMUTH_LLM_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=120
# BISMUTH_LLM_ABSOLUTE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=180

# Repair attempts when a model returns output that will not validate. Small local
# models need these; set to 0 in development to make violations fail loudly.
# BISMUTH_LLM_MAX_SCHEMA_RETRIES=2
